WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.440
- There are over a billion people on earth

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:04.550
that don't have access to clean water,

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:07.250
and you're complaining the
your Instagram's not growing?

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:08.193
Fuck you.

00:00:09.305 --> 00:00:11.888
(gentle music)

00:00:17.008 --> 00:00:18.140
You've just got to be thankful,

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:21.080
like, people just don't have perspective.

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:22.460
It's really easy to be energized

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:24.350
when you actually understand the score.

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:25.340
The problem is,

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:27.150
is that people just don't
have a perspective, right?

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:28.610
They don't understand that it's impossible

00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:30.040
to be a human being.

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:32.840
Like, it's impossible, like
that's the rarest in the world,

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:33.673
and so they...

00:00:33.673 --> 00:00:35.990
just people taking for
granted, you know, it's...

00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:37.710
you're more likely to
win the lottery 10 times

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:38.543
than be alive?

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.210
400 trillion to one,

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:44.733
that's how rare it is to be a human being.

00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:47.210
Everybody in this room is likely

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:49.260
to get hit by lightning seven times,

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:51.770
more likely than being
alive, that's crazy.

00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:55.800
Perspective, and once you see
gratitude and opportunity,

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:56.850
life is fun.

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:59.150
You get to decide if you're gonna dwell,

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:00.640
and play prevent defense,

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:03.800
or if you're going to see
opportunity and be grateful,

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:05.285
and go on offense.

00:01:05.285 --> 00:01:08.630
(gentle music)

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:13.000
I'm inspired by practicality
and reality and the truth,

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:15.310
which is it is ridiculously impossible

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:17.840
to become a human being, I am one.

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:20.370
I have other good things
going for me as a human being,

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:21.970
and I'm just grateful.

00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:25.150
You're dwelling and looking
at what you don't have,

00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:26.530
versus looking at what you have.

00:01:26.530 --> 00:01:28.170
There's nothing you'll ever accomplish

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:30.210
that's more remarkable
than that you have a chance

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:31.440
to accomplish something.

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:34.883
When you're so grateful for
the addback, you're happy.

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:39.423
But people dwell about dumb shit.

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:44.953
What's something you think
most people take for granted?

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:49.750
Family time, your health,
you know, living in America,

00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:51.650
access to clean water, food on the table,

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:52.850
a roof over your head.

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:54.590
I'm grateful for everything I have.

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:57.550
We lack gratitude, you
understand that, right?

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.260
I'm trying to get people to practice

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:00.660
reframing their perspective.

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:03.340
I practice gratitude every day.

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:06.570
If I wake up in the morning
and nobody I love passed away,

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:08.600
or came down with a terminal illness,

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:10.283
then my day starts off great.

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:14.580
If there was a list that
ranked everyone on earth

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:16.740
in terms of overall success and happiness,

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:20.860
from one to 7.7 billion,
where do you think you'd rank?

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:23.350
And this is really it for
me, this is really it.

00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:27.550
If you actually asked me why
I'm so damn happy all the time,

00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:29.560
I play this game all the time.

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:32.700
When I'm anxious, when I'm
upset about something silly,

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:35.793
because I'm a human, where do I rank?

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:42.380
When they live in London,
Dubai, or Los Angeles,

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:45.690
you're living amongst the
wealthiest of the wealth.

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:47.850
And you're looking at a very narrow window

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:49.770
of, like, well, my neighbor has this.

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:53.327
But you haven't taken it
all the way up and said,

00:02:53.327 --> 00:02:56.600
"Look how grateful I
should be for what I have."

00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:58.160
I love when people are
like, "Easy for you now."

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:00.380
No, from the get.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:02.150
I cried when I got two star wars figures,

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:03.410
instead of one when I was six,

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:04.760
'cause I couldn't believe
my parents could afford

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:05.710
to do that.

00:03:05.710 --> 00:03:09.610
Like, I'm grateful, I'm
grateful, gratitude, gratitude.

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:12.400
Like, somebody's always got it worse.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:13.700
That's how I think about this.

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:15.260
You have to stay grateful.

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:17.230
You can't take things for granted.

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:20.750
We have so much abundance in
the world, so much opportunity,

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:23.920
and too many people are crying
about what they don't have,

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:27.031
instead of being so deeply
grateful for what they have.

00:03:27.031 --> 00:03:30.300
(gentle music)

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:33.253
No, really, just stop right
now, take a deep breath.

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:36.580
I'm not kidding, take a deep breath.

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:40.456
Do it, respect it, have gratitude.

00:03:40.456 --> 00:03:43.039
(gentle music)

